      "solution": "goblin_count, round_count = map(int, input().split())\ncoins = list(map(int, input().split()))\npayers = []\nfor _ in range(round_count):\n    richest = coins.index(max(coins))\n    payers.append(richest)\n    coins[richest] //= 2\nprint(*payers)\n",
      "statement": "There are [[goblin_count]] goblins, each with an integer amount [[coins]]. Their indices go from {{0}} to [[goblin_count]] - {{1}}.\n\nFor each of [[round_count]] rounds, the dragon chooses the goblin with the <<largest current [[coins]]>>. Ties choose the <<smallest [[index]]>>.\n\nThe dragon takes half of the chosen goblin's [[coins]], <<rounding the payment up>> to an integer. Update that goblin's [[coins]] before the next round. For example, a goblin with {{9}} pays {{5}} and keeps {{4}}.\n\nPrint the chosen [[index]] for each round.",
